'''''Arum hygrophilum''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Araceae]].<ref name=KewPOWO>{{cite web|url= https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:86037-1|title= Arum hygrophilum Boiss.|author=<!--Not stated-->|date=n.d.|website=Plants of the World Online|publisher=The Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew|access-date= August 26, 2020}}</ref> It has a [[disjunct distribution]], found in northern and central [[Israel]], western [[Jordan]], [[Lebanon]], southwestern [[Syria]], eastern [[Cyprus]], western Turkey, and northeastern [[Morocco]].<ref name = powo>{{cite web |title=''Arum hygrophilum'' Boiss. |url=https://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:86037-1 |website=[[Plants of the World Online]] |publisher=[[Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew]] |access-date=18 March 2026}}</ref>
<ref>[http://apps.kew.org/wcsp/namedetail.do?name_id=16171 Kew World Checklist of Selected Plant Families]</ref><ref>Govaerts, R. & Frodin, D.G. (2002). World Checklist and Bibliography of Araceae (and Acoraceae): 1-560. The Board of Trustees of the Royal Botanic Gardens, Kew.</ref><ref>Dobignard, D. & Chatelain, C. (2010). Index synonymique de la flore d'Afrique du nord 1: 1-455. Éditions des conservatoire et jardin botaniques, Genève. 
</ref>

It is threatened by agricultural development and urbanization.<ref name="iucn status 19 November 2021" />

==Description==
By relative inflorescence height, ''Arum'' species are divided into "cryptic" species, whose inflorescences are borne on a short peduncle amid or below the leaves, and "flag" species, whose inflorescences are above leaf level at the end of long peduncles. ''A.&nbsp;hygrophilum'' is a flag species.{{sfn|Gibernau|Macquart|Przetak|2004|p=152}}

The species has a white inner spathe, which has purple accents. The small spadix is a dark purple color.

